CAT = "zare5Disclosure"; SEG = "DIS"
Q = [
("Under the General Code of Conduct, a provider must render financial services:",
 "Honestly, fairly and with due care", ["As quickly as the client asks", "Only in writing to every client", "In line with supplier targets"],
 "The general duty in the Code is to act honestly, fairly, with due skill, care and diligence, and in the interests of clients and the integrity of the industry."),
("The General Code of Conduct says a provider must act in the interests of:",
 "Clients and the industry", ["The product supplier above all", "Its shareholders above all", "Its compliance officer above all"],
 "The general duty of a provider is to act in the interests of clients and the integrity of the financial services industry."),
("Information given to a client under the Code must be:",
 "Correct and in plain language", ["Given only after the sale", "Written in strict legal terms", "Limited to a single printed page"],
 "Representations and information must be factually correct, in plain language, avoid uncertainty or confusion and not be misleading."),
("Under the Code, the required information about the provider, if given to a client orally, must be confirmed in writing within:",
 "30 days", ["7 days", "14 days", "90 days"],
 "Section 5 of the Code requires the provider's details, where given orally, to be confirmed in writing within 30 days. The same applies to the product supplier details in section 4."),
("When a provider gives a client a projection of a product's future value, it must:",
 "State the assumptions behind it", ["Guarantee the projected value", "Show only the best case", "Avoid giving any figures at all"],
 "Projections must make clear the underlying assumptions, so the client can see they are not guaranteed."),
("Under the Code, a conflict of interest is any situation in which a provider:",
 "Has an interest that may sway it", ["Has more than one client", "Sells one supplier's products", "Charges the client a fee for advice"],
 "A conflict of interest is an actual or potential interest that may influence the objective performance of obligations to a client, or stop the provider giving an unbiased and fair service."),
("How must a provider deal with a conflict of interest?",
 "Avoid it, or mitigate it", ["Disclose it only on request", "Refer it to the Ombud", "Simply note it in the client file"],
 "The Code requires a provider to avoid conflicts, and where that is not possible, to mitigate them and disclose them to the client."),
("Every FSP must adopt, maintain and apply:",
 "A conflict of interest policy", ["A client loyalty and rewards programme", "A sales target plan per product", "A commission sharing policy"],
 "The Code requires each provider to have a conflict of interest management policy that says how it identifies, avoids and mitigates conflicts."),
("An FSP's conflict of interest management policy must be:",
 "Published and open to clients", ["Kept only at the FSCA", "Shown only in its annual report", "Released only on a court order"],
 "The provider must publish its conflict of interest management policy in an appropriate manner so that clients and the public can see it."),
("Which financial interest may a provider receive?",
 "Commission authorised by law", ["A holiday from a supplier for sales", "Shares from a supplier for volume", "A bonus for selling one fund"],
 "A provider may receive commission authorised under the insurance or medical schemes laws, fees agreed in writing with the client, and a few other listed interests. Rewards for favouring a supplier or volume are prohibited."),
("A fee that the client specifically agreed to in writing, for a specific service, is:",
 "A permitted financial interest", ["Prohibited by the Code", "Allowed only for Category II", "Allowed only from suppliers"],
 "Fees specifically agreed to by the client in writing, and stoppable at the client's discretion, are among the financial interests the Code allows."),
("A provider may compare different financial products for a client only if it:",
 "Makes their differences clear", ["Names the cheapest one first", "Uses the supplier's own wording", "Gets the Authority's consent"],
 "Section 4(4) of the Code allows a comparison of products, suppliers or providers only if the differing characteristics of each are made clear, and bans inaccurate, unfair or unsubstantiated criticism."),
("A product supplier offers a representative a prize for reaching a sales target on one of its products. The representative may:",
 "Not accept it", ["Accept it if it is disclosed", "Accept it once a year", "Accept it if clients agree"],
 "A provider may not accept a financial interest that gives it an incentive to prefer quantity of business over quality of service, or one supplier's products over another's."),
("A provider must tell clients if it holds more than what share of a product supplier whose products it offers?",
 "10%", ["1%", "25%", "50%"],
 "Section 4(1)(d) of the Code requires a provider to disclose whether it directly or indirectly holds more than 10% of the relevant product supplier's shares, or an equivalent substantial financial interest."),
("A provider must disclose whether, in the previous 12 months, it received more than what share of its total remuneration from one product supplier?",
 "30%", ["10%", "50%", "75%"],
 "Under section 4(1)(d) of the Code, a provider must disclose that it received more than 30% of its total remuneration, including commission, from the product supplier during the preceding 12 months."),
("Which detail about the provider must be given to a client?",
 "Its contact and licence details", ["Its staff turnover rate", "Its owner's home address", "Its profit for the financial year"],
 "The Code requires the provider's name, contact details, legal status, licence categories and similar information so the client knows who they deal with."),
("A provider must tell the client whether it holds:",
 "Professional indemnity cover", ["A bank overdraft facility", "Shares in listed companies", "A fleet of company vehicles"],
 "The client must be told whether the provider holds any guarantees or professional indemnity or fidelity insurance cover."),
("Before rendering a financial service, a representative must give the client:",
 "Their name and their FSP", ["Their personal tax number", "Their own home address", "Their regulatory exam score"],
 "A representative must disclose their name and contact details and that they act on behalf of the FSP, which accepts responsibility for them."),
("A representative who does not yet meet the competence requirements must tell the client:",
 "That they are supervised", ["That they failed matric", "How much salary they earn", "Which clients they serve"],
 "A representative acting under supervision must disclose this, with the supervisor's details."),
("When recommending a product, the representative must disclose:",
 "Its fees and commission", ["The supplier's share price", "The supplier's staff numbers", "Other clients' product choices"],
 "The client must be told the nature and amount of fees, charges and any commission or consideration related to the product."),
("Which product details must a representative point out to a client?",
 "Exclusions and waiting periods", ["The supplier's marketing plans", "The representative's sales target", "Rival suppliers' share prices"],
 "Concise details of special terms, exclusions, waiting periods, loadings, penalties, excesses and restrictions must be disclosed."),
("Which right must a representative tell a client about when it applies?",
 "Any cooling-off right", ["A right to free extra cover", "A right to the supplier's dividends", "A right to choose the representative's fee"],
 "Where a product has a cooling-off right, the representative must tell the client about it and how to use it."),
("Fees, charges and commission must be disclosed:",
 "In rand amounts where possible", ["As a percentage only, never rand", "Only after the sale", "Only if the client asks"],
 "Amounts must be given in specific monetary terms; if an amount cannot reasonably be worked out in advance, its basis of calculation must be described."),
("A fee cannot be worked out in advance. The provider must:",
 "Describe how it is calculated", ["Leave it out until it is known", "Quote the highest possible fee", "Ask the supplier to explain later"],
 "When an amount is not reasonably pre-determinable, the Code requires its basis of calculation to be adequately described."),
("Required disclosures must be made to a client:",
 "In time for an informed decision", ["Within 30 days after the sale", "Only once a year, in a statement", "Only at policy renewal"],
 "Disclosures must be given timely, leaving the client reasonably sufficient time to make an informed decision."),
("A provider asks a client to sign away a right the Code gives them. The waiver is:",
 "Void", ["Valid if in writing", "Valid if witnessed", "Valid for business clients"],
 "Section 21 of the Code: no provider may request or induce a client to waive any right or benefit under the Code, or accept or act on such a waiver, and any such waiver is null and void."),
("An advertisement for a financial product must not:",
 "Mislead or deceive", ["Name the product supplier", "State the FSP's licence status", "Use plain language"],
 "Section 14 of the Code: an advertisement must not contain any statement, promise or forecast that is fraudulent, untrue or misleading. Naming the supplier and stating licence status are expected."),
("An advertisement that quotes a product's past performance must:",
 "Warn it is no guarantee", ["Show only the best year", "Be approved by the Ombud", "Promise similar returns"],
 "Section 14 of the Code: an advertisement with information about past performance must contain a warning that past performances are not necessarily indicative of future performances."),
]
